(ryoku/hub/quickshell/art/caracalla.png) is derived from "Caracalla MAN
Napoli Inv6033 n01" by Marie-Lan Nguyen
(https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caracalla_MAN_Napoli_Inv6033_n01.jpg),
a photograph of the Caracalla Farnese bust in the Museo Archeologico
Nazionale, Naples, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 2.5
Generic licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/). It was
upscaled, cut from its background, scaled down and cropped to the marble, as
on ryoku.dev. The credit shows beside the statue on Home and in Settings,
About, Credits.

The plates at the head of Ryoku Settings' pages
(ryoku/hub/quickshell/art/plates/) are derived from ryoku.dev's sculpture
plates, which are photographs on Wikimedia Commons: "Laocoon Pio-Clementino
Inv1059-1064-1067 n6", "Thermae boxer Massimo Inv1055 n7" and "Herakles
Farnese MAN Napoli Inv6001 n11" by Marie-Lan Nguyen (CC BY 3.0, CC BY 2.5
and CC BY 2.5), "Belvedere Torso, Hellenistic period, Vatican Museums (1)"
by Richard Mortel (CC BY 2.0), "Gianlorenzo bernini, ratto di proserpina,
1621-22, 05 mano nella carne" by Sailko (CC BY 3.0), "'David' by
