Parts of ryoget, the download engine in ryoku/shell/ryoget, are adapted from
Prism (prism-download-manager) by Jan Sechovec
(https://github.com/FortoGraphy/prism-download-manager) at commit d252535.
internal/httpdl/ takes its segmented transfer from prism-engine: bounded
ranged requests, range splitting and racing a slow tail, ramping up
connections and learning each host's limit, jittered backoff and Retry-After,
checking free space and preallocating the file, syncing before the resume
sidecar is written, the checks before a resume and reusing the final URL.
internal/engine/categories.go takes prism-core's file-type table and folder
choice, and internal/engine/checksum.go prism-engine's file hashing and the
check after the file lands. internal/media/challenge.go takes the cf-mitigated
bot-check signal, internal/links/pattern.go the range parsing,
internal/ytdlp/jsruntime.go prism-video's handling of yt-dlp's JavaScript
runtime, and internal/media/services/linkedin.go prism-core's list of LinkedIn
listing pages. It is a modified version: the Rust is rewritten in Go inside
ryoget, and Prism's desktop interface, browser extension, clipboard watcher,
scheduler, SQLite store and self-updater are left out. Copyright (c) 2026 Jan
Sechovec and Prism contributors. It is released under the MIT License, whose
text is in ryoku/shell/ryoget/LICENSE.prism and which the ryoku-shell package
installs as /usr/share/licenses/ryoku-shell/LICENSE.prism. That license is
compatible with Ryoku's GPL-3 distribution.
